1
00:00:02,994 --> 00:00:05,687
Hi! Today's trick
is the "hand wheel walk",

2
00:00:05,753 --> 00:00:08,713
where you walk
on the tire with your hands.

3
00:00:08,793 --> 00:00:21,168
[Music]

4
00:00:21,234 --> 00:00:25,181
The secret to this trick
is to create a forward imbalance

5
00:00:25,247 --> 00:00:28,928
and then make up for it
by moving forward.

6
00:00:28,994 --> 00:00:32,408
My first piece of advice
is not to be afraid of falling forward.

7
00:00:32,474 --> 00:00:34,814
At the start of every session,

8
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:37,624
I used to make myself fall forward once
to see that it wasn't scary

9
00:00:37,690 --> 00:00:40,433
and that I could handle the fall.

10
00:00:45,271 --> 00:00:49,697
The first step: move forward normally,
creating that forward imbalance.

11
00:00:50,491 --> 00:00:54,497
I think the most important thing
is to put a lot of weight on the saddle

12
00:00:54,563 --> 00:00:55,691
and very little on the tire.

13
00:00:56,637 --> 00:00:59,671
As for your legs, don't worry
about height at first,

14
00:00:59,823 --> 00:01:04,090
go for width to get more range,
and keep them straight.

15
00:01:04,156 --> 00:01:11,605
[Music]

16
00:01:11,671 --> 00:01:14,384
Once that starts working,
try lifting your legs,

17
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:17,617
which creates even more imbalance
and makes it much smoother.

18
00:01:18,477 --> 00:01:22,277
To do this, press your stomach
even harder into the saddle,

19
00:01:22,344 --> 00:01:24,550
pointing your heels up.

20
00:01:24,623 --> 00:01:34,038
[Music]

21
00:01:34,104 --> 00:01:36,625
The last step,
purely for looks,

22
00:01:37,050 --> 00:01:40,631
is to try to bring your torso
closer to the tire,

23
00:01:40,757 --> 00:01:43,946
pressing your stomach
even harder into the saddle,

24
00:01:43,970 --> 00:01:46,090
and lifting your legs
until your back is almost arched...

25
00:01:47,764 --> 00:01:52,957
This makes you lean even further forward
so your body slopes down more.

26
00:01:53,029 --> 00:02:01,168
[Music]

27
00:02:01,227 --> 00:02:03,668
Finally, if you want to go further,

28
00:02:04,681 --> 00:02:09,820
keep in mind that for any trick
with this saddle position,

29
00:02:09,886 --> 00:02:15,314
the advice is the same:
"one-hand wheel walk" or "hand pedaling",

30
00:02:15,381 --> 00:02:16,700
it's the same thing,

31
00:02:16,766 --> 00:02:19,830
and these are the steps
to repeat every time. There you go.

32
00:02:19,896 --> 00:02:32,550
[Music]

